A||||8||FieroGTChile||GT sail panel removal and installation||||1||
Z||000000||FieroGTChile||09-21-2001||02:27 AM||||Hi, could someone please tell me the specifics for removing and installing the sail panel(passenger side) on my '87 gt?<P>------------------<BR>Maroon '87 GT<BR>Gold '87 SE(Incapacitated)||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||09-21-2001||04:30 AM||||Just rip out the old sail panel.  Damn good chance it'll break anyway.  Make sure you remove <B>all</B> of the old adhesive, install the new adhesive (double sided tape) and carefully press the new sail panel in place.  That's what I did with mine (007Dougs tinted sail panels) except I accidentally mounted mine about a 1/4" too low.||||reg||1
Z||000002||MinnGreenGT||09-21-2001||11:52 AM||||Wait... sail panel or 1/4 window?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||09-21-2001||07:15 PM||||Same thing, aren't they?  Window looking thing, sort of triangular on the upper rear sides of the fastback?  FieroGTChile--If you were referring to something else, please disregard my instructions.||||reg||1
Z||000004||MinnGreenGT||09-22-2001||12:35 AM||||MM... isn't the phrase "sail panel" usually used to refer to the actual body work- the part that defines a "fastback" or a "notchback"... or maybe my brain is toast.||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroGTChile||09-22-2001||02:54 AM||||Thanks, I did mean the windows and it was very easy except that the window came out in about 500 different pieces and one of them gave me a nice cut.<P>------------------<BR>Maroon '87 GT<BR>Gold '87 SE(Incapacitated)||||reg||1
Z||000006||Monkeyman||09-22-2001||08:51 AM||||Oops.  I forgot to tell you that you should wear some gloves.  The original sail panel can be very sharp.  I wish I would have been able to save the passenger side on mine.  It was perfect.  I tried and ended up with confetti anyway.<P>MinnGreenGT--I wasn't trying to be an ass. ||||reg||1
